WEBVTT

00:04.000 --> 00:05.140
<i>Forbidden Instruments.</i>

00:06.560 --> 00:11.310
<i>Merely possessing these sorcery tools 
grants might approaching that of a witch.</i>

00:06.690 --> 00:11.570
<b>Forbidden Instruments</b>

00:12.320 --> 00:16.700
<b>Sorcery Tools</b>

00:12.480 --> 00:16.990
<i>But while their wielders gain power,</i>

00:17.530 --> 00:23.330
<b>Payment</b>

00:17.680 --> 00:23.330
<i>they must make sacrifices in payment
or else forfeit their lives.</i>

00:24.120 --> 00:27.610
<i>Thus, the use of Instruments 
is strictly forbidden.</i>

00:24.290 --> 00:33.510
<b>Sacrifice</b>

00:28.480 --> 00:32.080
<i>Yet those who turn to them 
are never in short supply.</i>

00:32.860 --> 00:34.180
<i>For you see...</i>

02:11.990 --> 02:13.180
What was that sound?

02:13.700 --> 02:15.360
Did you hear something?

02:15.840 --> 02:16.580
Yeah.

02:17.500 --> 02:19.050
I'm going home.

02:19.050 --> 02:20.660
If you're worried, I can walk you.

02:20.870 --> 02:23.700
I'll be fine. It's not far.

02:23.700 --> 02:24.600
Goodnight.

02:35.770 --> 02:38.090
<i>There sure are a lot of crows.</i>

03:23.000 --> 03:26.260
Not yet. It's still not enough.

03:27.000 --> 03:29.500
I've got to add more.

03:30.560 --> 03:35.900
The Witch's Pastime:
Opening Act

03:35.900 --> 03:39.110
Hey. Is there a witch around here?

03:42.190 --> 03:46.490
Beats me. They're supposed 
to tell us the details in person.

03:49.330 --> 03:52.980
So what would you like us to do this time?

03:52.980 --> 03:55.550
Please keep this between us,

03:55.550 --> 03:58.930
but the master of the house 
has a penchant for collecting.

03:59.450 --> 04:03.880
And I'm ashamed to say that a specimen
 has escaped from his collection.

04:04.190 --> 04:07.120
Escaped? So it's an animal?

04:07.120 --> 04:11.100
Yes, sir. And quite a violent one at that.

04:12.560 --> 04:15.790
It has claimed many victims already.

04:17.300 --> 04:22.620
Since you called in the Order, 
I assume it's not just a rare creature.

04:23.070 --> 04:26.160
Don't tell me you have a magical beast here.

04:28.800 --> 04:29.500
Yes.

04:29.920 --> 04:32.580
As you say, the creature is magical.

04:39.410 --> 04:42.390
So you want us to subdue that thing?

04:42.390 --> 04:46.930
You are to recapture it with the
 utmost haste, and without harming it.

04:46.930 --> 04:48.910
Without harming it?

04:48.910 --> 04:51.420
I see. That explains why you're struggling.

04:52.200 --> 04:54.640
Hm? Where are you going, Guideau?

04:54.640 --> 04:57.480
I'm done with this bullshit.

04:57.480 --> 04:59.360
Now, now. We're on the clock.

04:59.610 --> 05:02.530
As if I care about a plain old beast.

05:02.530 --> 05:04.990
You can handle the pet-sitting.

05:05.260 --> 05:06.660
Dear me.

05:07.130 --> 05:10.200
Who do you think you are, a king?

05:16.080 --> 05:18.790
Excuse me. Pardon the intrusion.

05:19.250 --> 05:22.840
Matter manipulation is the 
most basic of magic spells,

05:22.840 --> 05:25.760
but controlling fluids 
requires a particular knack.

05:26.220 --> 05:29.510
Honestly, I've always struggled with it.

05:30.880 --> 05:32.100
You're full of it.

05:32.340 --> 05:34.290
You wound me, Guideau.

05:34.830 --> 05:38.110
It's not nice to call people liars.

06:09.600 --> 06:11.350
Will that do?

06:15.870 --> 06:18.020
Splendid work.

06:18.340 --> 06:20.860
I was right to call on you.

06:21.270 --> 06:22.810
We're honored.

06:22.810 --> 06:26.180
Magical beasts are illegal 
in this country, you see.

06:26.180 --> 06:28.200
I wanted to handle this quietly.

06:28.640 --> 06:33.000
I heard that you'd take on any job,
 and I see that info was correct.

06:33.000 --> 06:34.990
Oh, not quite.

06:35.380 --> 06:40.360
We only stick our noses into magical trouble.

06:42.960 --> 06:47.170
An occult organization of magic, 
by magic, for magic.

06:47.680 --> 06:52.570
If you have any more difficulties, 
call the Order of Magical Resonance.

06:59.030 --> 07:02.810
Treating oneself after work
 sure hits the spot.

07:04.160 --> 07:06.220
What's wrong? Not eating anything?

07:07.290 --> 07:08.780
Gimme a break.

07:10.920 --> 07:13.950
Tell me what our last job was, jackass.

07:14.490 --> 07:20.360
We apprehended a petty burglar who had
committed heinous crimes using magic.

07:20.360 --> 07:22.580
Quite a good deed, if I do say so.

07:22.580 --> 07:24.080
And before that?

07:24.080 --> 07:27.550
We exterminated a ghastly tree 
that fed on magical power.

07:27.550 --> 07:28.710
And before <i>that</i>?

07:28.710 --> 07:31.450
Let me think...

07:31.450 --> 07:34.300
Oh, yes. A stalker abusing magic—

07:34.300 --> 07:35.260
Before that?!

07:35.260 --> 07:37.430
Babysitting a young magical beast.

07:38.930 --> 07:40.630
Are you screwing with me?

07:40.630 --> 07:44.960
What the hell do you think 
I joined your shitty Order for?

07:44.960 --> 07:48.310
You don't need to remind me.

07:48.660 --> 07:51.280
Oh, dear. That was good wine.

07:51.280 --> 07:53.300
Hurry up and find me a witch!

07:53.300 --> 07:55.990
If you can't do that, 
the Order's a waste of my time.

07:56.160 --> 08:01.370
You must realize that cases 
involving witches don't grow on trees.

08:01.370 --> 08:05.000
And our relationship is give and take.

08:05.000 --> 08:08.500
In exchange for our full support 
in achieving your goal,

08:08.500 --> 08:11.720
you agreed to serve 
at the Order's discretion.

08:11.720 --> 08:16.000
We get priority when witch cases comes up.

08:16.000 --> 08:19.160
So until one does, do your job.

08:19.580 --> 08:21.390
If you slack off like you did today,

08:21.390 --> 08:24.560
we won't give you witches, 
fine food, or anything else.

08:27.120 --> 08:30.690
You didn't need me today, anyway.

08:31.120 --> 08:32.200
True enough.

08:33.120 --> 08:34.150
Excuse me, sir.

08:35.320 --> 08:37.240
I was asked to give you this.

08:37.860 --> 08:38.950
Thank you.

08:41.840 --> 08:43.080
It's from the Order.

08:43.080 --> 08:45.670
Is it a witch?! Gimme!

08:47.200 --> 08:52.080
How many times must I tell you? You need 
an Order signet ring to break this seal.

08:55.090 --> 08:58.690
Although you should have 
one of these brands, too.

09:02.980 --> 09:05.390
Oh? Cheer up, Guideau.

09:05.780 --> 09:08.230
Speak of the devil.

09:27.920 --> 09:28.630
A witch!

09:28.840 --> 09:31.350
This lady is merely our client.

09:31.350 --> 09:33.480
So where's the damn witch, then?!

09:33.480 --> 09:36.090
We represent the 
Order of Magical Resonance.

09:36.090 --> 09:38.430
I believe you have a job for us?

09:38.430 --> 09:42.460
I'm sorry to have you come 
all this way. Please come in.

09:44.240 --> 09:48.980
I can't seem to open this case anymore. 
Can you do something about it?

09:53.560 --> 09:57.280
I see. A runic inscription.

09:57.760 --> 10:01.750
You're in luck. 
Undoing spells is my specialty.

10:01.750 --> 10:02.620
Goodness.

10:14.000 --> 10:18.170
Then what was that 
"Speak of the devil" about?

10:20.800 --> 10:24.430
Get ready for what's coming to you, asshole.

10:25.040 --> 10:28.140
I never said anything about a witch, did I?

10:28.680 --> 10:31.860
You should have realized that
when I left the coffin behind.

10:32.120 --> 10:34.520
Then what was that 
"Speak of the devil" about?

10:34.890 --> 10:38.860
I was just saying that you should 
take non-witch cases seriously.

10:38.860 --> 10:40.300
Bullshit!

10:40.300 --> 10:43.650
If you feel you were fooled, 
consider it a learning experience.

10:43.650 --> 10:45.370
It taught you a lesson.

10:45.370 --> 10:50.250
Like hell I will. 
Trusting you was my big mistake.

10:50.250 --> 10:53.570
"Mistake" is another word for "experience."

10:53.570 --> 10:55.460
They're both shortcuts to wisdom.

10:55.970 --> 10:58.660
Sorry, but we don't have time to argue.

10:58.660 --> 11:01.090
Our next job just came in.

11:01.700 --> 11:05.230
Hope for better luck on this one.

11:06.540 --> 11:09.470
I'll let it slide, but only for the time being.

11:09.470 --> 11:13.150
As soon as my curse has been lifted
 and I don't need the Order anymore,

11:13.750 --> 11:16.270
the first thing I'm gonna do is kill you.

11:16.960 --> 11:18.240
Glad to hear it.

11:18.980 --> 11:23.300
I'm looking forward to that day myself.

11:27.980 --> 11:32.900
A peaceful, witch-free month
 has passed since then.

11:32.900 --> 11:35.450
What a tranquil afternoon.

11:36.180 --> 11:40.570
I'd say the day you reclaim your 
real body is still a long way off.

11:40.570 --> 11:44.340
I'll kill you later, 
but I can always kick your ass now.

11:44.340 --> 11:46.850
Temper, temper.

11:47.310 --> 11:49.680
Anyway, eat your fill.

11:49.680 --> 11:50.770
Good, isn't it?

11:50.770 --> 11:52.140
It's gross as hell.

11:54.070 --> 11:56.890
For you, mister.

11:56.890 --> 11:58.600
From the Order again?

11:58.600 --> 11:59.280
Yes.

11:59.280 --> 12:02.330
More busy work, I bet.

12:02.330 --> 12:04.700
To hell with that crap. Rip it up.

12:05.440 --> 12:08.540
No, you'll like this one, Guideau.

12:09.960 --> 12:11.790
It came in a black envelope.

12:12.540 --> 12:14.420
So what?

12:14.900 --> 12:22.010
They only send these when a witch 
is involved and central to the case.

12:22.610 --> 12:28.730
It seems a witch is committing serial 
murders in Hayden, the capital of Pheres.

12:28.730 --> 12:33.350
They even make a point of 
calling the case "grotesque."

12:33.350 --> 12:34.260
Besides which—

12:34.260 --> 12:36.020
Enough. Gimme.

12:36.430 --> 12:38.320
You're so impatient.

12:40.980 --> 12:42.720
We're about to be busy.

12:42.720 --> 12:45.240
There's an ocean between us and this case.

12:45.580 --> 12:46.830
Pack your bags.

12:51.920 --> 12:54.250
<i>So a witch </i>and<i> a grimoire?</i>

12:56.670 --> 12:59.630
<i>We won't have an easy time of it.</i>

13:07.150 --> 13:09.010
Ms. Haines, it's dangerous!

13:09.010 --> 13:11.220
My children are in there!

13:11.440 --> 13:13.820
Shulk! Loran!

13:24.360 --> 13:26.240
You were groaning in your sleep.

13:26.760 --> 13:28.260
Are you okay?

13:28.260 --> 13:30.300
Yeah, I'm fine.

13:30.710 --> 13:32.200
If you say so.

13:39.580 --> 13:42.700
Sorry. She gave us the slip again.

13:43.180 --> 13:44.240
How many dead?

13:44.800 --> 13:46.720
At least five.

13:47.120 --> 13:49.630
And the bodies were...

13:51.220 --> 13:55.970
"Consumed, sacrificed, 
or something similar by a witch"?

13:56.950 --> 14:01.260
How could anyone do something 
so horrible? She must be crazy.

14:01.810 --> 14:03.940
"Crazy," huh?

14:05.040 --> 14:08.000
I've seen plenty of perps with a screw loose.

14:08.000 --> 14:10.140
They all had one thing in common.

14:10.690 --> 14:12.250
Know what that is?

14:12.250 --> 14:13.080
No.

14:13.440 --> 14:17.830
Unfulfilled desires born 
from a sense of inferiority.

14:18.350 --> 14:24.460
Losing control of them can turn even 
upstanding people into crazed villains.

14:24.830 --> 14:27.040
You mean no person is born evil?

14:27.760 --> 14:28.900
"Person," huh?

14:29.790 --> 14:31.700
Is a witch a person?

14:32.220 --> 14:33.640
Beats me.

14:33.640 --> 14:39.690
But witch or human, 
anyone who can do this must be scum.

14:40.450 --> 14:41.710
I couldn't agree more.

14:42.140 --> 14:44.760
We didn't expect this fight.

14:44.760 --> 14:48.320
Is that why you didn't set 
all your wards in time?

14:48.320 --> 14:50.970
You mean she wouldn't 
have escaped if I'd finished?

14:51.460 --> 14:52.210
Er, no.

14:53.090 --> 14:57.620
Closing off the scene would've made 
no difference. She slips through wards.

14:58.230 --> 14:59.350
What I meant was—

14:59.350 --> 15:00.570
I know.

15:01.200 --> 15:07.070
We need to box her in to make 
her cast as many spells as possible,

15:07.070 --> 15:09.170
or we'll never figure out her magic.

15:10.460 --> 15:13.350
But even if we solve that mystery, 
it's just the first step.

15:13.980 --> 15:18.010
The full force of the Hayden Police 
still has to take this slow and steady.

15:19.200 --> 15:23.660
A feeble police force can't 
fight a monster any other way.

15:24.190 --> 15:27.500
Ms. Haines, I shouldn't have to tell you

15:27.500 --> 15:31.150
that this goes way beyond 
regular serial murder.

15:31.900 --> 15:34.040
You're the only mage we've got.

15:34.600 --> 15:37.780
If you feel powerless, talk to the mayor.

15:39.700 --> 15:42.620
Witches are the Paladin Corps' jurisdiction.

15:42.960 --> 15:46.160
Unless something changes, 
the body count will just keep growing.

15:46.160 --> 15:47.380
I know.

15:49.830 --> 15:51.300
I know that.

15:55.940 --> 15:57.750
I know it's easier said than done,

15:57.750 --> 16:01.180
but try not to beat yourself up over 
what happened to Inspector Cole.

16:01.750 --> 16:04.880
I've handled plenty of horrific cases.

16:04.880 --> 16:08.020
I thought people always 
remembered the perpetrators

16:08.530 --> 16:12.280
and forgot the victims in no time.

16:12.840 --> 16:17.740
But then someone murdered 
people I cared about,

16:18.420 --> 16:21.390
and I realized that I'd never 
forget the names of either.

16:22.710 --> 16:26.290
Don't worry. I'll do my job.

16:35.300 --> 16:38.510
Oh, dear. It appears we're too late.

16:38.510 --> 16:42.850
Don't give me that crap. 
You let her slip right out from under us.

16:42.850 --> 16:44.610
Cut me some slack.

16:44.610 --> 16:49.250
And rest easy. The witch 
in this case will be back.

16:50.710 --> 16:56.530
Grotesque mass murder committed by
 a witch, a.k.a. the "Witch's Pastime" case.

16:56.530 --> 17:00.830
As of last week, the victims 
numbered 36, including police officers.

17:00.830 --> 17:02.330
Quite a tough nut to crack.

17:02.880 --> 17:05.870
What did tonight make the body count?

17:06.880 --> 17:08.740
Who are you two?

17:09.230 --> 17:11.920
You're saying things 
I don't want to think about,

17:12.430 --> 17:14.590
so I guess you know who I am.

17:15.130 --> 17:17.010
And you look suspicious.

17:17.440 --> 17:19.760
What's in that coffin?

17:19.760 --> 17:22.380
Grilling us already?

17:22.380 --> 17:24.160
Well, I can't blame you.

17:24.580 --> 17:28.060
Rest assured, we're perfectly respectable.

17:28.650 --> 17:30.520
So please, stay your hand.

17:34.050 --> 17:36.420
We mean you no harm.

17:36.780 --> 17:39.070
In fact, we'd like to help you.

17:40.130 --> 17:41.280
Help how?

17:41.790 --> 17:45.070
The Order of Magical Resonance sent us.

17:45.070 --> 17:47.810
A major incident is disturbing your city.

17:47.810 --> 17:53.000
If you suspect a witch is responsible, 
then we have much to offer you.

18:02.480 --> 18:04.200
Hayden Police business.

18:04.200 --> 18:08.100
We'll take a table in the back, 
but I'd like to set a soundproof ward.

18:08.100 --> 18:09.650
S-Sure.

18:10.760 --> 18:12.220
I got confirmation.

18:12.720 --> 18:16.360
It seems the mayor really did 
sign off on a request to the Order.

18:16.360 --> 18:19.290
I would never lie to a beautiful lady.

18:19.810 --> 18:24.700
By the way, could you hold off on that ward
 until we've ordered and gotten our food?

18:24.920 --> 18:28.290
Of course. At least let me
 have a cup of coffee.

18:28.290 --> 18:31.850
No, please wait for our full meal.

18:31.850 --> 18:33.760
Replacing wards is a hassle, no?

18:40.220 --> 18:44.060
For our part, we'd like to hear 
about the case as soon as possible.

18:44.570 --> 18:46.930
Tell me your story first.

18:46.930 --> 18:50.850
You may have the mayor's approval, 
but I don't trust you.

18:50.850 --> 18:53.120
But you have a witch case on your hands.

18:53.610 --> 18:55.950
Sooner or later, 
the Paladin Corps will step in.

18:55.950 --> 18:58.820
But for some reason, 
the mayor is stalling them.

18:59.170 --> 19:01.570
Making you our only hope?

19:01.570 --> 19:02.740
Looks that way.

19:03.320 --> 19:06.320
To begin with, 
this whole situation is strange.

19:06.320 --> 19:09.620
Police forces aren't 
equipped to combat witches.

19:09.620 --> 19:11.710
What you need is an army.

19:12.020 --> 19:16.690
That's why global peacekeepers 
like the Paladin Corps handle witches.

19:17.370 --> 19:21.520
The mayor is probably refusing their help

19:21.520 --> 19:24.350
to claim the glory of 
solving the case without them.

19:24.640 --> 19:28.940
Anyone can see how foolish that is, 
so why do you all go along with it?

19:29.470 --> 19:34.220
As the Hayden Police's only mage, 
I believe you're in charge of the case.

19:34.220 --> 19:37.110
You ought to protest. Why don't you?

19:39.650 --> 19:40.960
Who gives a shit?

19:40.960 --> 19:44.070
Just tell me everything 
you know about the witch.

19:44.070 --> 19:46.780
Then I'll kick all the witch ass you want.

19:47.470 --> 19:49.980
Why are <i>you</i> so fixated on the witch?

19:50.410 --> 19:53.370
Most people would steer clear 
of a witch serial killer.

19:53.750 --> 19:54.400
That's—

19:54.400 --> 19:56.220
Guideau, have a bone.

19:58.530 --> 20:01.280
For our organization, essentially.

20:01.280 --> 20:05.050
We collect the essence of magic. 
Witches, naturally, and—

20:05.050 --> 20:08.330
Don't hide anything unless 
you want to lose even more trust.

20:09.930 --> 20:12.440
I came up with this ward myself.

20:13.160 --> 20:16.560
Lies can't fool me inside it.

20:17.630 --> 20:18.780
Asshole.

20:21.090 --> 20:23.990
Dear me. How shrewd of you.

20:25.450 --> 20:26.700
Answer me.

20:32.960 --> 20:36.080
Well, our circumstances aren't worth hiding.

20:36.680 --> 20:39.920
We just want to undo a curse.

20:40.550 --> 20:41.630
A curse?

20:42.080 --> 20:45.220
A witch's curse. You must know of them.

20:45.220 --> 20:49.100
Sure. Anyone who's even 
dabbled in magic does.

20:49.360 --> 20:51.540
Then I'll be brief.

20:51.540 --> 20:53.940
My friend here is under a witch's curse.

20:55.160 --> 20:58.300
So we're looking for the 
witch who cast the curse.

20:58.300 --> 21:01.520
And more or less at random, 
since we have almost nothing to go on.

21:01.520 --> 21:03.150
That's not all.

21:03.150 --> 21:06.140
I'll find her and kill her.

21:06.140 --> 21:07.990
This is revenge.

21:08.870 --> 21:10.450
Revenge...

21:13.620 --> 21:15.870
I don't believe we're lying.

21:17.170 --> 21:18.040
Right.

21:19.290 --> 21:21.170
No, I believe you.

21:21.850 --> 21:24.040
You have extremely personal reasons,

21:24.040 --> 21:27.090
but I can trust them over 
great and noble causes.

21:27.090 --> 21:32.520
Oh? You need to use reasoning?
 I thought you could tell if we were lying.

21:32.520 --> 21:34.380
I lied about that.

21:34.980 --> 21:37.350
I can't cast a spell <i>that</i> good.

21:37.590 --> 21:39.400
What?! Screw you!

21:39.400 --> 21:40.710
All right, fine.

21:41.160 --> 21:43.260
I'll take your help.

21:44.150 --> 21:45.740
Our partnership starts tomorrow.

21:46.340 --> 21:48.220
Meet here at 9 AM.

21:51.280 --> 21:53.030
Hey, when you get down to it...

21:53.440 --> 21:56.840
She found out what we knew
 and gave us nothing.

24:01.110 --> 24:04.850
Now, shall we go see a witch?

24:05.590 --> 24:09.960
Next time: "The Witch's Pastime: Final Act."

24:05.710 --> 24:09.960
The Witch's Pastime

24:05.710 --> 24:09.960
Final Act
